    "articles": [
      {
        "no": 53,
        "text": {
          "en": "Interpretation of Paragraph 2 of Article 53 of the Basic Law of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the People's Republic of China\n(Adopted at the 15th meeting of the Standing Committee of the Tenth National People's Congress on 27 April 2005)\nThe 15th meeting of the Standing Committee of the Tenth National People's Congress deliberated the bill submitted by the State Council on requesting an interpretation of Paragraph 2 of Article 53 of the Basic Law of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the People's Republic of China. In accordance with Subparagraph (d) of Article 67 of the Constitution of the People's Republic of China and paragraph 1 of Article 158 of the Basic Law of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the People's Republic of China, and after consulting the Committee for the Basic Law of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress, the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress interprets the provisions of Paragraph 2 of Article 53 of the Basic Law of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the People's Republic of China as follows:\nParagraph 2 of Article 53 of the Basic Law of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the People's Republic of China provides: \"If the office of the Chief Executive becomes vacant, a new Chief Executive shall be selected within six months in accordance with the provisions of Article 45 of this Law.\" The expression \"a new Chief Executive shall be selected in accordance with the provisions of Article 45 of this Law\" covers both the selection of a new Chief Executive in accordance with the method for the selection of the Chief Executive prescribed in Article 45 of the Basic Law of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the People's Republic of China and the determination of the term of office of the new Chief Executive in accordance with the method for the selection of the Chief Executive prescribed in that Article.\nParagraph 3 of Article 45 of the Basic Law of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the People's Republic of China provides: \"The specific method for selecting the Chief Executive is prescribed in Annex I: Method for the Selection of the Chief Executive of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region.\" Article 1 of Annex I provides: \"The Chief Executive shall be elected by a broadly representative Election Committee in accordance with this Law and appointed by the Central People's Government.\" Article 2 provides: \"The term of office of the Election Committee shall be five years.\" Article 7 provides: \"If there is a need to amend the method for selecting the Chief Executives for the terms subsequent to the year 2007, such amendments shall be made with the endorsement of a two-thirds majority of all the members of the Legislative Council and the consent of the Chief Executive, and they shall be reported to the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress for approval.\" The above provisions show that, before the year 2007, under the institutional arrangement whereby the Chief Executive is elected by an Election Committee with a term of five years, if the office of the Chief Executive becomes vacant because the Chief Executive does not serve the full five-year term prescribed in Article 46 of the Basic Law of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the People's Republic of China, the term of office of the new Chief Executive shall be the remaining term of the former Chief Executive; and that, after the year 2007, if the above method for selecting the Chief Executive is amended, then, should the office of the Chief Executive become vacant, the term of office of the new Chief Executive shall be determined in accordance with the amended specific method for selecting the Chief Executive.\nIt is hereby announced."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 53."
        }
      }
    ]
