          "en": "Interpretation of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress\non the Application of the Subject of the Crimes of Dereliction of Duty in Chapter IX\nof the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China\n(Adopted at the 31st meeting of the Standing Committee of the Ninth National People's Congress on 28 December 2002)\nIn light of the situations encountered in judicial practice, the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress discussed the question of the application of the subject of the crimes of dereliction of duty in Chapter IX of the Criminal Law, and gives the following interpretation:\nPersons who engage in public service in an organisation that exercises the functions and powers of State administration in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations, or persons who engage in public service in an organisation entrusted by a State organ to exercise functions and powers on behalf of the State organ, or persons who, although not included in the staffing establishment of a State organ, engage in public service in a State organ, and who, when exercising functions and powers on behalf of a State organ, commit acts of dereliction of duty that constitute a crime, shall be investigated for criminal responsibility in accordance with the provisions of the Criminal Law on crimes of dereliction of duty.\nIt is hereby announced."
